        <abstract>
            <para>The Newberry College Herbarium houses over 21,000 vascular plant specimens collected predominantly in the Southeastern United States and especially in South Carolina and North Carolina. The collection is particularly notable for its large and varied holdings of regional rhodendrons.</para>
